# G081 — E-Card Generator

*v2. See `ecard.md` for prose: template-and-data as separation between
content and presentation, slot schema validated at creation not
render time, defaults materialised into cards, unknown placeholders
visibly preserved (fail loud), categories as cross-template axis.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Automated Birthday Card Mailer

[birthday-mailer
    IN ORDER TO
        pull the vault's contacts whose birthday is today
        fill a birthday template per person and send each one as HTML email
        so the only work left is picking the template and the phrasing

    @gallery <- [ecard[load-gallery]]

    every day at 08:00
        @birthdays <- [vault[query {filter: "birthday == today"}]]
        for @p in @birthdays
            @template <- [ecard[pick-template
                                  {gallery: @gallery,
                                   category: "birthday"}]]
            @card <- [ecard[create-card
                              {gallery: @gallery,
                               template-id: @template:id,
                               filled: {name: @p:name,
                                         age: "year " + @p:age-today + "!"},
                               recipient: @p:email,
                               sender: "the Vault"}]]
                || -> #card-invalid @resistance:reasons
            [email[send {to: @p:email,
                          subject: "Happy birthday!",
                          html: [ecard[render
                                         {gallery: @gallery,
                                          card-id: @card}]]}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[ecard
    load-gallery
    add-template      {gallery, template}
    pick-template     {gallery, category}
    create-card       {gallery, template-id, filled, recipient, sender}
                                                  ;; validates at creation
    render            {gallery, card-id}           ;; never fails on stored card
    render-plain      {gallery, card-id}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: validation `where` slots and filled agree

[ecard[create-card {gallery: @g, template-id: @tid, filled: @vals, ...}]
    IN ORDER TO
        reject any card whose filled data does not match the template schema
        so a stored card is always renderable and rendering never fails

    @template <- @g:templates at @tid

    @vals
        where key not in @template:slots            -> #unknown-slot
    @template:slots
        where slot:required and slot:name not in @vals and no default
                                                     -> #missing-required
        where slot:name not in @vals and default exists
                                                     -> materialise default into @vals
    otherwise
        -> store the card with @vals (all slots resolved at creation)
]

Defaults are copied, not looked up at render time. Template edits
don't retroactively change existing cards — each card is a
self-contained snapshot.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: unknown placeholders preserved `where` fail-loud

[ecard[render {gallery: @g, card-id: @id}]
    walk @template:html
    where placeholder is declared slot   -> substitute filled value
    where placeholder is reserved (_recipient, _sender) -> substitute card field
    where placeholder is unknown         -> leave {{placeholder}} in output
    IN ORDER TO
        make the template author's typo visible in the rendered output
        instead of silently producing "From ." in place of "From {{typo}}."
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @g <- [ecard[load-gallery]]
    [ecard[add-template
            {gallery: @g,
             template: {id: 1, category: "birthday",
                         slots: [{name: "name", kind: "Text", required: true}
                                  {name: "age", kind: "Text",
                                   required: false,
                                   default: "another year older"}],
                         html: "<p>Happy birthday, {{name}}! {{age}}</p>"}}]]

    @card <- [ecard[create-card
                      {gallery: @g, template-id: 1,
                       filled: {name: "Nathan"},
                       recipient: "n@example.com",
                       sender: "the Vault"}]]
    ;; age default materialised into the card

    -> [ecard[render {gallery: @g, card-id: @card}]]
    ;; -> "<p>Happy birthday, Nathan! another year older</p>"
]
